hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2842","**\nNarrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr (RA), who said:\n\nJibril (AS) came to Ibrahim (AS) and showed him the rites (of Hajj). He prayed with him the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers at Mina, then the Maghrib and 'Isha prayers at Mina as well. Then he went with him to 'Arafah, where he prayed with him the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers at 'Arafah. He made him stand at the standing place (of 'Arafah) until the sun set. Then he moved him forward, and he prayed with him the Maghrib and 'Isha prayers at Muzdalifah. Then he spent the night there. Then he moved him forward until he stoned the Jamarah. He then said to him, \"Now you know,\" and showed him all the rites. He did this with the Prophet (ﷺ)."
